{"title":"Orthocenter","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The <b>orthocenter</b> of a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangle</a> is the point of intersection of its <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitudes</a>.  It is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematical_convention\" title=\"Mathematical convention\"> conventionally</a> denoted <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/4/3b484374a3d190b7da30ce26d184e6ae3305e73c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(15cm); markscalefactor = 0.01; dot((0,0)); dot((4,0)); dot((3,3)); dot((3,0)); dot((2,2)); dot((3,1)); dot((3.6,1.2)); draw((0,0)--(4,0)--(3,3)--cycle); draw((0,0)--(3.6,1.2),red); draw((2,2)--(4,0),red); draw((3,0)--(3,3), red); draw(rightanglemark((0,0),(3,0),(3,1))); draw(rightanglemark((4,0),(3.6,1.2),(0,0))); draw(rightanglemark((0,0),(2,2),(4,0))); label(&quot;Orthocenter&quot;,(2.85,1.1),W); [/asy]\" width=\"712\" height=\"535\" />\nThe lines highlighted are the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">altitudes</a> of the triangle, they meet at the orthocenter.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Proof_of_Existence\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Proof of Existence</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Easier_proof\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Easier proof</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Properties\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Properties</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resources\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resources</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_Existence\">Proof of Existence</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of Existence\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>Note: The orthocenter's existence is a consequence of <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ceva%27s_Theorem\" title=\"Ceva&#39;s Theorem\">Ceva's Theorem</a> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://jwilson.coe.uga.edu/EMT668/EMAT6680.F99/Martin/proofs/proof5\">proof</a>). However, the following proof, due to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Leonhard_Euler\" title=\"Leonhard Euler\">Leonhard Euler</a>, is much more clever, illuminating and insightful.</i>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/d/67d616b35fc9702763fcb0b034d0d91933a6d069.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(8)); pair A=(8,7), B=(0,0), C=(10,0), A1 = (B+C)/2, O = circumcenter(A,B,C), G = (A+B+C)/3, H = 3*G-2*O; draw(A--B--C--cycle); draw(A--G--H--cycle); draw(A1--G--O--cycle); label(&quot;A&quot;,A,(0,1));label(&quot;B&quot;,B,(0,-1));label(&quot;C&quot;,C,(0,-1));label(&quot;G&quot;,G,(1,-1));label(&quot;H&quot;,H,(0,-1));label(&quot;O&quot;,O,(-1,1));label(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,A1,(0,-1));dot(H); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"488\" />\nConsider a triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> with <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">circumcenter</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">centroid</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/9/1090530ae883b627e090bfb5e450ef796febca40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"16\" /> be the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be the point such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46f2c6ec7efed35ced5ff6f2d772707c06cfd48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HG = 2 GO$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />.  Then the triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/61986fb9aca15a3d9fa47a37f10e6cc396e2ed1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AGH$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/c/c6c1f258ac097dd0ebea0184f2e36c0be00159b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A&#39;GO$\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Similar\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Similar\">similar</a> by side-angle-side similarity.  It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/3/bb3ddf9a5fa2fca5c4787d4f989af0eef1387bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AH$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> is parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86c25031c3faf302ad6810ea2ad713504e4d83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OA&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"16\" /> and is therefore perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />; i.e., it is the altitude from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.  Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/f/4bfc6159e268a0f5d736eca73477c99a13209da9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/e/20e8e26d580012b86d8fe55e70e5740908c35af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CH$\" width=\"31\" height=\"12\" />, are the altitudes from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/1716e238f553f7dabd85afad448d78d505bc0ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${C}$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />.  Hence all the altitudes pass through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.  Q.E.D.\n</p><p>This proof also gives us the result that the orthocenter, centroid, and circumcenter are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Collinear\" title=\"Collinear\">collinear</a>, in that order, and in the proportions described above.  The line containing these three points is known as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euler_line\" title=\"Euler line\">Euler line</a> of the triangle, and also contains the triangle's <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point\" title=\"De Longchamps point\">de Longchamps point</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nine-point_center\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Nine-point center\">nine-point center</a>.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Easier_proof\">Easier proof</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Easier proof\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>That seems somewhat overkill to prove the existence of the orthocenter. We use a much easier (and funnier) way.\n</p><p><br />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/2/8a2c792af0766241fc0335acb3dfe82c040858b4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]     import olympiad;     size(4cm);     pair A=dir(110), B=dir(200), C=dir(-20), D,E,F,H;     H=orthocenter(A,B,C);     D=B+C-A;     E=C+A-B;     F=A+B-C;     draw(A--B--C--A);     draw(D--E--F--D);     draw(A--H,dotted);     draw(B--H,dotted);     draw(C--H,dotted);     label(&quot;A&quot;,A,N);     label(&quot;B&quot;,B,dir(190));     label(&quot;C&quot;,C,dir(-10));     label(&quot;D&quot;,D,S);     label(&quot;E&quot;,E,dir(45));     label(&quot;F&quot;,F,dir(140));     label(&quot;H&quot;,H,dir(50)); [/asy]\" width=\"192\" height=\"148\" />\n</p><p><br />\nLet the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and the line through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> parallel to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/1/c61f1e8be9d73f590167b39417e42bbaa1787fe0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> Define <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/0/250f765e0f0b3842f9d095dc0a3569905d344ce8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> similarly. \n</p><p>(Alternatively, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> can be constructed by reflecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> across each of its edges' midpoints, respectively.)\n</p><p>Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/2/5c2d4444a2a124ff8478f8ec09208746866a2c69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FA=BC=AE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"135\" height=\"14\" /> (and likewise for the other sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />), and so each altitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> is a perpendicular bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Since the perpendicular bisectors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/2/872e3b09425c9659d782119a543dc858aa520a40.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle DEF$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> intersect (at its circumcenter), this intersection point is also the the intersection of altitudes of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, its orthocenter.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Properties\">Properties</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Properties\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li>The orthocenter and the circumcenter of a triangle are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Isogonal_conjugate\" title=\"Isogonal conjugate\">isogonal conjugates</a>.</li>\n<li>If a triangle is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Acute_triangle\" title=\"Acute triangle\">acute</a>, then its orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is in the triangle; if the triangle is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_triangle\" title=\"Right triangle\">right</a>, then  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is on the vertex opposite the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Hypotenuse\" title=\"Hypotenuse\">hypotenuse</a>; and if it is <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Obtuse_triangle\" title=\"Obtuse triangle\">obtuse</a>, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the triangle.</li>\n<li>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> its orthocenter. Then the reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> over <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />:</li></ul>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/3/d43dfa0aa5888fc748071e9fb210a3deee6c8212.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(8)); pair A=(8,7), B=(0,0), C=(10,0), H=orthocenter(A,B,C), A1, B1, C1; A1 = 2*foot(A,B,C)-H; B1 = 2*foot(B,C,A)-H; C1 = 2*foot(C,A,B)-H; draw(A--B--C--cycle,black+1); draw(A--A1);draw(B--B1);draw(C--C1); draw(A1--B--C1--A--B1--C--cycle); draw(circumcircle(A,B,C)); dot(A1^^B1^^C1^^H); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,(0,1));label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,(-1,0));label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,(1,0)); label(&quot;$A&#39;$&quot;,A1,(0,-1));label(&quot;$B&#39;$&quot;,B1,(1,1));label(&quot;$C&#39;$&quot;,C1,(-1,1)); label(&quot;$H$&quot;,H,(-1,-1)); [/asy]\" width=\"668\" height=\"648\" />\n</p>\n<ul><li>The reflections of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> over the midpoints of the sides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/6/5/e657259c0995d2c36d46744bb4aa81471e6575ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA$\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> are also on the circumcircle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />:</li>\n<li>The circumcircle and the nine-point circle are [homethy|homethetic] with respect to the orthocenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, with scaling factor equal to 2. That is, the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> and a point on the circumcircle is a point on the nne-point circle.</li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resources\">Resources</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resources\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Books/AoPS_B_Item.php?page_id=2\">Art of Problem Solving Volume 2</a> - Example 21-4\nEuclidean Geometry in Mathematical Olympiads by Evan Chen - Section 1.3\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Orthocenter&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Centroid\" title=\"Centroid\">Centroid</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Incenter\" title=\"Incenter\">Incenter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Altitude\" title=\"Altitude\">Altitude</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circumcenter\" title=\"Circumcenter\">Circumcenter</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=De_Longchamps_point\" title=\"De Longchamps point\">de Longchamps point</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.038 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 328/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 11692/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:3862:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018003045 and revision id 243158. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}